# Nowhere default apps (DIA-20260617-06) — pinned F-Droid versions.
#
# These APKs are NOT committed (~277 MB; Fennec alone is 120 MB) -- except WireGuard (see its row). fetch-default-apps.sh
# downloads them from F-Droid into this dir before a build; the Android.bp android_app_import modules then bake them into
# /product/app (presigned: F-Droid's own signature is kept, so F-Droid can update them in place later).
# ⚠ That in-place update works on Diaspore (LineageOS) ONLY. On Endospore GrapheneOS refuses every update of a
# system app that does not come from its first-party app source, so a bundled app there moves only when these
# pins move with a release (DECIDED 2026-09-24, NWP-20260924-05; docs/bundled-app-updates.md).
# Run `bash fetch-default-apps.sh` once on a fresh tree before `m systemimage`. (The committed FDroid.apk
# this line used to mention was removed in DIA-20260801-37.)
#
# Columns:  Name  Package  VersionCode  SHA256  [manual]
# A 5th column `manual` marks an APK that is NOT on F-Droid at its pin (NWP-20261011-22): fetch-default-apps.sh
# never builds an F-Droid URL for it. Present with the pinned sha -> skipped; absent or any other sha -> the fetch
# FAILS, printing the comment above the row, which must name where the APK comes from.
